#. mandela — Mindset Network launch speech, 16 July 2003
#. https://www.mandela.gov.za/mandela_speeches/2003/030716_mindset.htm
msgctxt "Labdoo education quotes"
msgid "Education is the most powerful weapon we can use to change the world."
msgstr "L’éducation est l’arme la plus puissante que nous puissions utiliser pour changer le monde."

#. mandela — Mindset Network launch speech, 16 July 2003
#. https://www.mandela.gov.za/mandela_speeches/2003/030716_mindset.htm
msgctxt "Labdoo education quotes"
msgid "Nelson Mandela"
msgstr "Nelson Mandela"

#. keller — Optimism: An Essay (1903)
#. https://www.gutenberg.org/cache/epub/31622/pg31622-images.html
msgctxt "Labdoo education quotes"
msgid "The highest result of education is tolerance."
msgstr "Le résultat le plus élevé de l’éducation est la tolérance."

#. keller — Optimism: An Essay (1903)
#. https://www.gutenberg.org/cache/epub/31622/pg31622-images.html
msgctxt "Labdoo education quotes"
msgid "Helen Keller"
msgstr "Helen Keller"

#. confucius — The Analects, II.15; translation by Leonard A. Lyall (1909)
#. https://www.gutenberg.org/cache/epub/24055/pg24055-images.html
msgctxt "Labdoo education quotes"
msgid "Learning without thought is naught; thought without learning is dangerous."
msgstr "Apprendre sans réfléchir est vain ; réfléchir sans apprendre est dangereux."

#. confucius — The Analects, II.15; translation by Leonard A. Lyall (1909)
#. https://www.gutenberg.org/cache/epub/24055/pg24055-images.html
msgctxt "Labdoo education quotes"
msgid "Confucius"
msgstr "Confucius"

#. aristotle — Metaphysics, I.1; translation by W. D. Ross
#. https://classics.mit.edu/Aristotle/metaphysics.1.i.html
msgctxt "Labdoo education quotes"
msgid "All men by nature desire to know."
msgstr "Tous les êtres humains désirent naturellement savoir."

#. aristotle — Metaphysics, I.1; translation by W. D. Ross
#. https://classics.mit.edu/Aristotle/metaphysics.1.i.html
msgctxt "Labdoo education quotes"
msgid "Aristotle"
msgstr "Aristote"

#. dewey — My Pedagogic Creed, article II (1897); excerpt from a sentence beginning “I believe that…”
#. https://cyc-net.org/cyc-online/cycol-0502-dewey.html
msgctxt "Labdoo education quotes"
msgid "Education, therefore, is a process of living and not a preparation for future living."
msgstr "L’éducation est donc un processus de vie et non une préparation à la vie future."

#. dewey — My Pedagogic Creed, article II (1897); excerpt from a sentence beginning “I believe that…”
#. https://cyc-net.org/cyc-online/cycol-0502-dewey.html
msgctxt "Labdoo education quotes"
msgid "John Dewey"
msgstr "John Dewey"

#. mann — Twelfth Annual Report, Massachusetts Board of Education (1848); excerpt
#. https://ushistory.education/historical-documents/horace-mann-twelfth-annual-report/
msgctxt "Labdoo education quotes"
msgid "Education, then, beyond all other devices of human origin, is the great equalizer of the conditions of men."
msgstr "L’éducation est donc, plus que tout autre moyen d’origine humaine, le grand facteur d’égalité des conditions humaines."

#. mann — Twelfth Annual Report, Massachusetts Board of Education (1848); excerpt
